{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778944152,"nonce":"Fcwq/t1PNcFizKHLDUGDvzEmFbI=","message":"## Addendum: Claude Code local-wrapper ToS review needed before public distribution\n\nMLL raised a specific product direction: Mandible may launch/wrap the user's local Claude Code CLI, watch local Claude Code history, and send input through a PTY/tmux-like interface, rather than relying only on the Claude Agent SDK.\n\nPreliminary legal/product reading as of 2026-05-16:\n\n- For Free/Pro/Max users, Claude Code is under Anthropic Consumer Terms; for Team/Enterprise/API users, Commercial Terms apply.\n- Claude Code docs say OAuth auth is intended for purchasers of subscription plans and native Anthropic applications, while developers building products/services that interact with Claude capabilities, including Agent SDK use, should use API-key auth through Console or supported cloud providers.\n- The same docs say third-party developers may not offer Claude.ai login or route requests through Free/Pro/Max plan credentials on behalf of their users.\n- A purely local wrapper that launches the user's installed `claude` binary, leaves auth inside Claude Code, and does not collect/host/route credentials looks materially different from a hosted service routing subscription credentials. Still, public distribution should be reviewed carefully.\n\nDesign recommendations for compliance-sensitive implementation:\n\n- Mandible should not ask users for Claude.ai credentials or OAuth tokens.\n- Mandible should not proxy Claude traffic through a Mandible-hosted service.\n- Mandible should launch the local `claude` CLI and observe local files/PTY output where permitted by local OS permissions.\n- Mandible should make clear that Claude Code usage remains subject to Anthropic's terms and the user's Claude Code authentication/account.\n- SDK/API-key mode should remain available and clearly distinct from subscription/OAuth CLI mode.\n- Before public release, re-check current Anthropic legal/compliance docs and Claude Code docs because this area is changing quickly.\n\nThis issue should remain the place to centralize public-release risk review for OAuth/SDK/CLI wrapping assumptions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}